ation citation-type="other">Elford, B.C. 1993. Generating viable extra-erythroytic forms of <italic>P. falciparum.  TDR News</italic> (WHO Bulletin) 41:11.</citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ferrari</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Cutler</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Uptake of chloroquine by human erythrocytes</article-title><source>Biochem Pharmacol</source><year>1990</year><volume>39</volume><fpage>753</fpage><lpage>762</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2306282</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="other">Ferrari, V., and D.J. Cutler. 1991. Simulation of kinetic data on the influx and  efflux of chloroquine by erythrocytes infected with <italic>Plasmodium falciparum.  Biochem. Pharmacol.</italic> 42 p. 167&#x02013;179.</citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fitch</surname><given-names>CD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title><italic>Plasmodium falciparum</italic>in owl monkeys: drug resistance and chloroquine binding</article-title><source>Science</source><year>1970</year><volume>169</volume><fpage>289</fpage><lpage>290</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4988896</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fitch</surname><given-names>CD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Chloroquine-resistant <italic>Plasmodium falciparum</italic>: differences in  the handling of [<sup>14</sup>C]-amodiaquin and [<sup>14</sup>C]-chloroquine</article-title><source>Antimicrob Agents  Chemother</source><year>1973</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>545</fpage><lpage>548</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4208293</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"